  "_comment": [
    "The 2026-09-03 outage. Not a reconstruction: every id, timestamp and sha",
    "below was read back out of the Actions API for this repo, and the two runs",
    "are the only two that had ever happened — the nightly odds run of",
    "09-02 13:40:56Z (4h25m after its 09:15 slot) and the market snapshot of",
    "09-03 00:58:32Z (1h58m after its 23:00 slot).",
    "",
    "Note the workflow `created_at` values: the API answers in the repo owner's",
    "offset (-04:00), not in Z. Reading those as UTC would move every 'live",
    "since' four hours and invent or hide a due slot, so this fixture keeps the",
    "form the API actually sends. The doc's 'live since' column is these times",
    "converted: 14:51:11-04:00 is 18:51:11Z.",
    "",
    "The crons are the ones live at the time — round minutes, before the",
    "odd-minute change shipped with the fix — so this fixture keeps testing the",
    "arithmetic of that morning even after the real schedules move again.",
    "",
    "`now` is 16:43Z, the first watchdog slot at which the dropped 09-03 09:15",
    "nightly slot has cleared a 6h grace. statcast-ingest and modal-refit had",
    "not had a single slot come due, which is why `run_number: 1` on all four",
    "workflows was not the total failure it looked like."
  ],
